  "result": "The decision is made in `src/hooks/shortcut-match.ts`:\n\n- **`prefersMetaKey(platform)`** decides what \"mod\" means. It returns true on Mac, iPhone, iPad and iPod, where \"mod\" means Command (Meta). Everywhere else it means Control.\n- **`matchesShortcut(keys, event, platform)`** checks whether a key press matches a shortcut. It reads the shortcut's keys with `parseShortcut`, turns \"mod\" into Command or Control using the rule above, and then requires the pressed key and all four modifiers (Ctrl, Meta, Alt, Shift) to match exactly.\n\n`src/hooks/use-keyboard-shortcut.ts` only listens for key presses and hands each one to `matchesShortcut`. It doesn't make the decision itself.\n\nANSWER: src/hooks/shortcut-match.ts",
